ntdll: Test only the byte of NtQueryDirectoryObject's BOOLEAN arguments.

A PE caller built with clang sets a BOOLEAN stack argument with a byte store
and leaves the other seven bytes of the slot as it found them, which the
Windows x86-64 ABI permits (GCC happens to write 32 bits). Wine's syscall
dispatcher copies the slot whole into the SysV argument register, and a unix
side built with clang then tests the low 32 bits, because clang as a SysV
callee assumes the caller zero-extended a char. With stale bytes above the
BOOLEAN, `restart` reads as TRUE on every call, the cursor never advances, and
GetLogicalDrives() re-reads entry 0 of \DosDevices forever. Measured on
Steam's MachineIDInfoThread and on steamwebhelper's ThreadPoolForegroundWorker
against Wine 11.0 from crossover-sources-26.3.0; see docs/steam-login.md.

An empty asm with the argument as an in/out operand makes the compiler treat
it as a fresh 8-bit value, so it tests the byte and nothing above it.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c
@@ -2081,9 +2081,15 @@
                                         ULONG *context, ULONG *ret_size )
 {
     unsigned int status, i, count, total_len, pos, used_size, used_count, strpool_head;
-    ULONG index = restart ? 0 : *context;
+    ULONG index;
     struct directory_entry *entries;
+
+    /* A PE caller may set a BOOLEAN with a byte store and leave the rest of the
+     * slot stale; the dispatcher passes the slot as is, and a clang-built callee
+     * would test 32 bits of it. Look at the byte only. */
+    __asm__( "" : "+r" (single_entry), "+r" (restart) );
 
+    index = restart ? 0 : *context;
     if (!(entries = malloc( size ))) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
 
     SERVER_START_REQ( get_directory_entries )
